# OctoAcme Project Management Docs

## Project Management Process Summary

OctoAcme uses a lifecycle-based, cross-functional approach: initiatives begin with a clear problem, measurable outcome, stakeholder alignment, and go/no-go decision; approved work is planned into a prioritized backlog with ownership, estimates, dependencies, release milestones, and Definition of Done; delivery teams execute through visible project boards, small pull requests, CI, testing, reviews, and regular progress and risk reviews; releases follow pre-release, deployment, verification, rollback, and communication practices; and retrospectives turn lessons into tracked, owned improvements.

